+    Enlarging the neighborhood beyond 2-swap lets the descent escape swap-only
+    local optima (relocation shifts a whole run of positions, a move no single
+    swap reproduces), so it converges to an equal-or-better local optimum. The
+    steepest (most-improving) feasible move is applied each sweep; only strictly
+    improving moves are accepted, so the objective is monotonically non-increasing."""
     n = len(perm)
